     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This question has also been asked on stackoverflow <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/39843561/error-in-importing-a-new-python-module-in-knitr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/39843561/error-in-importing-a-new-python-module-in-knitr&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792354774509000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2UFSYkfICDMOR5roWPJXSX\">here</a>.  <div><br></div><div><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">I want to use a python engine in <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);white-space:pre-wrap\">knitr</code>. I have installed a module named <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);white-space:pre-wrap\">undaqTools</code> for python 2.7 using Anaconda3. If I run the following in IPython, it works fine:</p><pre style=\"padding:5px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(16,16,148)\">from</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> undaqTools </span><span style=\"color:rgb(16,16,148)\">import</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(43,145,175)\">Daq</span></code></pre><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">I tried the same in a python code chunk but that didn&#39;t work. I found a relevant question in SO, linked<a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/30172948/knitr-error-when-importing-python-module\" style=\"color:rgb(0,89,153)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/30172948/knitr-error-when-importing-python-module&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792354774509000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3CKEKknlkeiMHAAG46wrPR\">here</a>. So, I first did following in IPython:</p><pre style=\"padding:5px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(16,16,148)\">import</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> undaqTools\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(16,16,148)\">import</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> os\r\npath </span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> os</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">path</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">dirname</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">undaqTools</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">__file__</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">\r\npath\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(43,145,175)\">Out</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(125,39,39)\">5</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">]:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(125,39,39)\">&#39;C:\\\\Anaconda3\\\\envs\\\\py27\\\\lib\\\\site-packages\\\\undaqtools-0.2.3-py2.7.egg\\\\undaqTools&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">  </span></code></pre><p style=\"font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Therefore, I created a new chunk in knitr and did following:</p><pre style=\"padding:5px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);color:rgb(57,51,24);word-wrap:normal\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;DejaVu Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\"><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">```{</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">python</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">}</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(16,16,148)\">import</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\"> sys\r\nsys</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">path</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">append</span><span style=\"color:rgb(48,51,54)\">(</span><span style=\"color:r